# Keeps the build context to the source that actually ships.
#
# Without this, `COPY . .` pulls in the developer's .venv (360MB) and type
# caches (47MB) and layers them on top of the venv the image builds for
# itself — which is both wasted space and a correctness hazard, since the
# host venv contains macOS binaries that cannot run in the container.

.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage

# Tests and their fixtures are not needed to serve the API. CI runs the
# suite against the repo, not against this image.
tests/

.python-version
README.md
*.md
